From 5a2b5e40855329b5d1ebbfc5a375b7857d990e89 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sukrit Jaidee <45908411+SukritJaAIproject@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 11:40:05 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 22/25] feat(desktop): v4 research grid gains the replayed
 ISO-2 + SLAC arm

The v4 research grid had no ISO 15118-2 arm. The ISO 15118 edition's own
held-out replay (v4 weights, ISO-2 rules + SLAC 600 ms together,
D:/ev_ai_stage/v4_iso, 2026-09-24) now fills a new arm, "iso2normative",
rescored under all three label profiles by
ev_charger_ai/benchmark/research_grid_from_cache.py replay-arm v4-iso into
results/research_grid_v4_iso.json and generated into research-data.ts.

- It is a replay, so every model is exact - AI Agent included - and it
  carries no projection footnote. strict.iso2normative equals the ISO
  edition's bundled leaderboard to 1e-9; RL is unchanged in every profile.
- The ISO 15118 edition opens the research panel on this arm, so its first
  view is its own leaderboard (strict: TraditionalAI 77.3, MultiAgent 72.5,
  AgenticAI 70.9, AI Agent 68.9). Baseline editions still open on + SLAC
  600 ms.
- ISO-2 alone stays unmeasured for v4; the 2026-09-12 set never ran ISO-2
  and SLAC together, so that tab is disabled for it with the visible reason.
  The subtitle says which ISO-2 results a grid has (alone / combined / none).

Tests: 16 files / 299 pass; tsc adds no error.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
